---
title: Zucchini Crisp
description: Oversized zucchini, peeled and boiled with lemon and cinnamon, bakes into a mock apple crisp.
tags: [crisp, baking, late-summer]
course: dessert
icons: [cucumber, wheat, oven]
cuisine: American
source:
  name: Down Redbud Drive
  author: Victoria Pruett
  url: https://www.downredbuddrive.com/zucchini-crisp-mock-apple-crisp/
servings: 12
time: 1h20m
---

> **Picking the Zucchini** — Use an oversized zucchini, the kind left in the garden too long, until the flesh firmed up. Tender ones hold more water, so you may need to drain some of the liquid after boiling.

= Filling

Peel the @zucchini{8%cup}(about 1 oversized, measured after slicing). Cut it in half lengthwise and scrape out every seed with a spoon. Slice 1/4 inch thick, like apples for a crisp.

Combine the zucchini, @granulated sugar{150%g}(3/4 cup), @lemon juice{1/4%cup}, @ground cinnamon{1%tbsp}, and @water{3/4%cup} in a #large pot{} and stir until the zucchini is coated. Bring to a boil over high heat, then boil for ~boil{15%minutes}, stirring occasionally. It won't look like enough liquid to boil, but it is. Meanwhile, heat the oven to 375°F (190°C).

= Topping

Mix the @butter{225%g}(16 tbsp, softened), @quick oats{90%g}(1 cup), @brown sugar{213%g}(1 cup, packed), @all-purpose flour{180%g}(1 1/2 cups), and @&ground cinnamon{1%tbsp} in a #bowl{} with a fork. It will look thick.

= Bake

Pour the zucchini into a greased #9-by-13-inch baking pan{}. Sprinkle the topping evenly over the surface with your fingers.

Bake uncovered until the edges just start to turn golden brown, ~bake{55-60%minutes}.

> **Serving** — Serve warm with vanilla ice cream.
